<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yamacraw</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Yamacraw were a small Native American band formed in the 1720s by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muscogee">Creek</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yamasee">Yamasee</a> people under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tomochichi">Tomochichi</a>, living at Yamacraw Bluff on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/savannah">Savannah</a> River. Their friendship with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-oglethorpe">James Oglethorpe</a> allowed the English to found Savannah there in 1733. After Tomochichi's death in 1739 the band merged back into the Creek.</p></div>
